<article class="env-lemma" id="05528B">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05528B">Lemma <span data-tag="05528B">6.5.3.4</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be an $\infty $-topos, and let $U_{\bullet }$ be a simplicial object in $\calX $. Let $L: \calX \rightarrow \calX ^{\wedge }$ be a left adjoint to the inclusion. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The simplicial object $U_{\bullet }$ is a hypercovering of $\calX $. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
The simplicial object $L \circ U_{\bullet }$ is a hypercovering of $\calX ^{\wedge }$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $L$ is left exact, we can identify $L \circ \cosk _{n} U_{\bullet }$ with $\cosk _{n} (L \circ U_{\bullet })$. The desired result now follows from Remark <a href="/tag/4D5F0A" data-tag="4D5F0A">6.5.2.18</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>